Am Montag, 1. Juli 2002 23:08 hast du geschrieben:
> just look at the many packages around on ctan with copyright notices =
of
> some sort (prior to lppl) that are "authorless" by now.

Don't think about packages prior to lppl because the problem will stay =
there
even after changing lppl.

Current lppl already gives a chance to friendly overtake an unsupported
package: rename it. They main problem may be the organization. If e.g. a
package at CTAN would be moved from /supported/foo to /other/foo or even
/obsolete/foo and a file would be created /supported/foo/see_newfoo this =
may
be an improvement.

BTW: I really know the problem of "how to find the author and what to do =
after
not finding him" because I've had it when I started with KOMA-Script in =
1994.

Gru=DF
Markus

